course: dictionary
lesson: 11964
title: Catastrophic: a word for disasters
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Catastrophic means causing terrible damage, harm or suffering. It is another word for a disaster. «The flood was catastrophic, and many families lost their homes.» The clues are lost homes and suffering, so catastrophic must mean very, very bad.
explain: Scientists and historians use catastrophic for big events such as floods, earthquakes, fires and storms. Some scientists think a catastrophic asteroid hit may have ended the dinosaurs. Here the word is serious, not silly.
explain: People also say catastrophic in a joking way to exaggerate. «My cake fell on the floor. It was catastrophic!» Nobody was hurt, so the word is funny and over the top. Ask yourself: is this a real disaster, or is someone being dramatic?
explain: To check the meaning, swap in a word like disaster or terrible damage. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Catastrophic is an adjective, and it can be spelled catastrophic in both its forms: more catastrophic.
fact: «Catastrophic» means causing terrible damage, harm or suffering.
fact: A catastrophic event is a disaster, such as a huge flood, earthquake or fire.
fact: People sometimes use «catastrophic» as a joke to say something went very wrong, like a messy cake.
fact: Words like «minor» mean the opposite: not very serious.
exercise: «The flood was catastrophic, and many families lost their homes.» What does catastrophic mean here? | *Causing terrible damage and suffering | Good for a picnic | Very small and quiet | Slightly wet
exercise: «My cake fell on the floor. It was catastrophic!» Why might someone say this? | Because a real earthquake shook the kitchen | Because the cake was perfect and won a prize | *To exaggerate in a joking way about a messy mishap
exercise: «The earthquake was catastrophic, but the tremor after it was minor.» Find and copy the word that means not very serious. | *minor | tremor | catastrophic | earthquake
test: «The fire was catastrophic, so the town needed help from far away.» What does catastrophic show about the fire? | *It was a disaster that caused great harm | It was a warm, sunny day | It was a small, cosy campfire
test: Which sentence uses catastrophic as a joke? | «The flood was catastrophic for the whole village.» | *«My sandwich was catastrophic, so I dropped it in a puddle and laughed.» | «The storm was catastrophic and tore down the trees.» | «The asteroid was catastrophic for the dinosaurs.»
exam: Which way is a good check for the meaning of catastrophic in a sentence? | Count how many letters it has | Find a word that rhymes with it | Skip it, because it never matters | *Swap in disaster or terrible damage and see if it still makes sense
